The following splits use ConcatDataset (multiple entities concatenated): TRAIN, VAL, TEST

Why this matters:
  - Each entity has its own scaler (mean/std) fitted on its data
  - ConcatDataset loses track of which sample came from which entity
  - Denormalized metrics use only the first entity's scaler
  - This gives INCORRECT results for samples from other entities

Normalized metrics are consistent with training but mix
different real-world scales across entities.

